      "card_ids": ["C09", "C55"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Imipramine-N-oxide, a tricyclic propylamine derivative, showed ~100% oral systemic availability versus IV, supporting high oral absorption for the query's propylenediamine/indane scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C10", "C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Donepezil, which contains an indane/indanone motif, has ~100% human oral bioavailability; dog/rat values of 28-41% remain above the 20% threshold, and a vague formulation-limitation statement does not outweigh direct human absolute F measurements.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C11", "C33", "C49", "C64", "C36"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Urapidil, an aromatic amine with a propylamine-type linker, has absolute oral bioavailability of 72-78% in humans, supporting high F for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C04", "C01", "C20", "C69"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Laquinimod (80-90%), oxcarbazepine/licarbazepine (89%), tiracizine (34%), FK788 (55% human), and moexipril (22%) are all at or above the 20% threshold in their most relevant human measurements.",
      "card_ids": ["C23", "C03", "C17", "C06", "C12"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low L2 values (benazeprilat <7% and poor oral bioavailability; dog 2.57%, cat 3.2%; FK788 rat 9.6%) are not transferable to the query: benazeprilat is a polar dicarboxylic acid/zwitterion whose 27-28% F was achieved only via the prodrug benazepril, and FK788's low value is species-specific.",
      "card_ids": ["C38", "C50", "C32", "C45", "C08", "C43", "C48"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No transferable context provides affirmative evidence for F < 20% in a lipophilic basic diamine; the query's dicationic ionization is a physicochemical uncertainty, not an endpoint outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C09", "C10", "C04", "C07"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C32", "C33", "C35", "C36", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C44", "C45", "C48", "C49", "C50", "C51", "C52", "C53", "C54", "C55", "C57", "C58", "C60", "C63", "C64", "C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C69", "C70", "C71", "C72", "C73", "C74", "C75", "C76"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule; all support is transferred from structurally related basic amines.",
    "The query is fully ionized (dicationic) at physiological pH; no direct permeability or first-pass data quantify the impact of the second positive charge on F.",
    "The benazeprilat context is confounded by prodrug administration and inconsistent (C08 27-28% vs C43 >=17%); its low parent F is not transferable to a lipophilic diamine.",
    "Species differences (e.g., FK788 rat 9.6% vs human 55%; donepezil dog/rat 28-41% vs human ~100%) limit quantitative transfer.",
    "Moexipril L2 range 13-22% is threshold-adjacent, but the L1 gold is 22% and the context is a polar prodrug ester, limiting transfer.",
    "No context exactly matches the N-phenyl-N-indanyl propylenediamine scaffold."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 adds mixed context: many high-F human records for lipophilic basic amines and some low-F records for non-transferable acids/species. The most transferable evidence still supports F >= 20%, and no affirmative threshold-relevant low evidence applies to the query. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

